+
+### Client source registration
+
+`registerWorkspaceSource(ctx, source)` composes source-adapted Workspace rows with the local catalog and routes identity-bearing commands to their owning `IWorkspaces` adapter. Sources must translate all Workspace and Session identities before registration and before remote dispatch. Cross-source reorder/move operations are refused. Registration validation failures roll back rows, keys and identity reservations. Invalid updates from an accepted source withdraw that source and report a diagnostic, preserving local operation; its identities remain reserved until Controller disposal. Registration follows the contributing Cordis fiber; withdrawal removes rows and subscriptions while reserving its key and identity predicates until the Controller is disposed, so stale identities cannot fall back to the local Host. Root create/default initialization remain local. Source availability must be enforced by the adapter; merged lifecycle/error fields continue to describe the local catalog. This extension does not install Session source routing or render a remote Workspace by itself.
